### How that ISC notice was arrived at — read this before relying on it

The upstream repository ships **no** license text: no LICENSE file in the
repository, and none in its published npm package either (the tarball of
`@nloui/paperless-mcp@1.0.0` contains eight files — six `src/*.js`,
package.json and README.md). What it does declare is `"license": "ISC"` and
`"author": "Nick Loui"` in its package.json, unchanged from its first commit
(2024-12-27) to today.

So there is no upstream copyright notice to preserve verbatim, and the one
above is a **reconstruction**, not a quotation: the name comes from that
`author` field, the years from the range of upstream's commits (2024-12-27 to
2025-11-11), and the license text below is the canonical ISC text rather than
anything upstream published.

